      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:212:13",
      "text": [
        " أَنَّ عَلِيّاً صَلَوَاتُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ كَانَ يَكْرَهُ الْحَجَّ وَ الْعُمْرَةَ عَلَى الْإِبِلِ الْجَلَّالَاتِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "MuhammadBin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Al Hassan Bin Musa, from Giyas Bin Kaloub, from Is’haq Bin Ammar, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Ja’far<sup>asws</sup>, from his<sup>asws</sup> forefathers<sup>asws</sup> that Ali<sup>asws</sup> disliked the Hajj and the Umra to be performed upon the camels feeding on dung’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "13. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn Ahmad from al-Hassan ibn Musa from Ghiyath ibn Kalub from Ishaq ibn ‘Ammar who has said the following: “Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has narrated from his ancestors who have said that Ali, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, disliked performing al-Hajj or al-‘Umrah on a camel that ate feces.’” (Fatwa best explains Hadith 12-13 of this Chapter) "
        ]
      }
    },
